## Harness overhead replay

| client | case | conc | exact distribution replay | scalar s median | SHA-256 s median | combined s median |
| --- | --- | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
{% for row in aggregate %}
| {{ row.client }} | {{ row.case }} | {{ row.concurrency }} | {{ row.overhead.complete and row.overhead.distribution_complete }} | {{ value(row.overhead.scalar_only_s_median, 6) }} | {{ value(row.overhead.sha256_only_s_median, 6) }} | {{ value(row.overhead.combined_s_median, 6) }} |
{% endfor %}

Replay runs separately on the observed size histogram, in sorted size order, with explicit byte/chunk/bin limits. It estimates harness costs under synthetic memory/cache conditions. Replay values are never subtracted from measured load. Diagnostic trace and profiler runs are excluded from control comparisons.

For duration windows the exact distribution is replayed in at most 64 segments, each respecting the existing byte/chunk limits. Segment histograms, timing sums and coverage of all observed bytes/chunks are checked; an incomplete replay cannot qualify.

